# 1. docker compose up -d
# 2. F5 (both projects start)

@api = https://localhost:7138

### Q1 - what are the most borrowed books?
GET {{api}}/api/books/most-borrowed?limit=5

### Q1 narrowed to a window (half-open: includes 2025-09-01, excludes 2026-01-01)
GET {{api}}/api/books/most-borrowed?limit=5&from=2025-09-01&to=2026-01-01

### Q2 - which patrons borrowed the most in a given time frame?
GET {{api}}/api/patrons/most-active?limit=5

### Q3 - reading pace. Loan 18 was held exactly one day.
GET {{api}}/api/loans/18/reading-pace

### Q3 - loan 19 was held 36 hours, so the pace uses a day and a half.
GET {{api}}/api/loans/19/reading-pace

### Q3 - loan 29 has not come back yet: 409.
GET {{api}}/api/loans/29/reading-pace

### Q4 - what else did the people who borrowed this title borrow?
GET {{api}}/api/books/1/borrowed-together?limit=5

### Q4 - a book that is not in the catalogue: 404.
GET {{api}}/api/books/999/borrowed-together

### A limit outside 1-100: 400.
GET {{api}}/api/books/most-borrowed?limit=0

### Lend a book
POST {{api}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patronId": 6,
  "bookId": 5
}

### Send it again - 409, the patron already has it
POST {{api}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patronId": 6,
  "bookId": 5
}

### Take the loan id from the 201 and bring the book back
POST {{api}}/api/loans/31/return

### Fetch a loan
GET {{api}}/api/loans/31
